{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Aggregate Reference by Identity.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Aggregate Reference by Identity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"aggregate reference by identity aggregate reference by identity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Aggregate Reference by Identity.md","fileName":"Aggregate Reference by Identity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Aggregate Reference by Identity","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-22 20:53\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Aggregate Consistency and Persistence]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Aggregate Consistency and Persistence","Aggregate","Consistency Boundary","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Aggregate Reference by Identity.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Aggregate Reference by Identity.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"aggregate reference by identity aggregate reference by identity","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Aggregate Reference by Identity.md","fileName":"Aggregate Reference by Identity.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Aggregate Reference by Identity","heading":"Aggregate Reference by Identity","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Aggregate reference by identity stores the identifier of another [[Aggregate]] instead of holding a navigable object reference to it. This makes the [[Consistency Boundary]] explicit: loading one aggregate does not silently load or lock another, and no database foreign-key graph implies that both must change together. Coordination across the identities occurs in the application workflow or through events. Some information may be duplicated when a local snapshot is needed, with synchronization handled explicitly.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Aggregate Consistency and Persistence","Aggregate","Consist